      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's perfectly normal to feel stressed when something unexplained affects your everyday life. If you're concerned about managing your energy levels, techniques such as mindfulness meditation, deep breathing exercises, or yoga can be helpful in calming your nervous system and potentially reducing the intensity of emotional outbursts. Mental and emotional regulation techniques are a recognized way to help people manage stress and emotions. Additionally, ensuring you're getting enough sleep, maintaining a healthy diet, and staying hydrated can support your overall well-being and could potentially decrease the frequency of these incidents. Keeping a journal to note when these episodes happen might help identify patterns or additional stressors that you can work on independently of the office situation. Remember, reaching out to a professional therapist or counselor is always a good way to address these sorts of concerns. You're not alone, and there are strategies you can try to regain a sense of control and peace.",
